===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|UK|Ireland|Commonwealth|dated|_|in North America|}} A period of 2 [[weeks]].
#: {{nearsyn|en|halfmonth}}
#* {{RQ:Orwell Down and Out|chapter=1|passage= On being kicked the girl fell desperately in love with Henri, and for a '''fortnight''' they lived together and spent a thousand francs of Henri's money.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Benjamin Welles|title=A Hot Potato for Nixon|work=The New York Times|date=1969-01-12|url=https://www.nytimes.com/1969/01/12/archives/a-hot-potato-for-nixon.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=The “lame duck” Johnson Administration, in its final '''fortnight''' in office, grappled last week with a diplomatic hot potato in the form of the latest Soviet proposal for a “just and lasting” Middle East peace settlement.}}

